0353+  6BB1             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0354+  6BB1             ; DSK_CHANGE_DIR_U: Change the current directory
0355+  6BB1             ;                   and update config files and work area
0356+  6BB1             ;
0357+  6BB1             ; This one is tricky. We can't update CURDIR until after we are sure that
0358+  6BB1             ; the directory change has been sucessful, but if we update a config file
0359+  6BB1             ; after setting our directory then it won't be set anymore! Also if we fail
0360+  6BB1             ; we should restore the previous directory.
0361+  6BB1             ;
0362+  6BB1             ; Thus we do it like this:
0363+  6BB1             ;
0364+  6BB1             ; 1. Read current content of CURDIR, save in memory
0365+  6BB1             ; 2. Set CURDIR contents to the directory we want to change to
0366+  6BB1             ; 3. Try to change to the directory, if successful, we're all set
0367+  6BB1             ; 4. On error changing the directory, set CURDIR to its previous contents
0368+  6BB1             ;    and change to it again
0369+  6BB1             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0370+  6BB1             ; Input:  HL = Directory path, "dir/dir2/dir3", no starting or ending "/"
0371+  6BB1             ;         A  = 0 for relative to current, 1 for absolute
0372+  6BB1             ; Output: A  = 0: Ok
0373+  6BB1             ;              1: Other error
0374+  6BB1             ;              2: Directory not found
0375+  6BB1             ;              3: It's a file, not a directory
0376+  6BB1             ;              4: Path is too long
